    "Description": "OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssh: Local MITM of X11 forwarding via abstract UNIX socket pre-binding in Red Hat Enterprise Linux OpenSSH client versions (CVE-2026-55655)\n\n* openssh: Double free in Red Hat Enterprise Linux versions of OpenSSH DH-GEX client path during FIPS known-group validation leads to client-side denial of service (CVE-2026-55653)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: sftp client allows attacker to control downloaded file location (CVE-2026-59995)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH sshd: Security bypass due to incorrect handling of forwarding and tunneling options (CVE-2026-59999)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Information disclosure via shared compression side-channel (CVE-2026-106582)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: Credential disclosure via failed GSSAPI authentication (CVE-2026-106553)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Denial of service via oversized decompressed packets (CVE-2026-106585)\n\n* openssh: openssh: Command injection via unvalidated command-line username (CVE-2026-106583)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
